# /etc/containers/systemd/vmscontroller.container — the controller: one per
# box (one per cluster in М11). Stateless — restart it freely. No port:
# nothing asks it anything. Its token writes placement only — vms/workers/*,
# vms/placement/*, vms/slots/*, the snapshot — and never a camera's row.
# ================================================================================================
# NOTES — what every part of this file does and why (kept beside the code, not in a separate document)
# ================================================================================================
# # vmscontroller.container — the controller: one per box, stateless, no port, the only writer of placement
#
# **Role.** The Quadlet unit for `vmscontroller` at `/etc/containers/systemd/vmscontroller.container` (one per
# box; one per cluster in М11). It runs `python3 -m vms controller`: the placement pass every five seconds —
# `ensure_placed`, `redistribute`, `publish_snapshot`. Stateless, restart it freely; nothing asks it anything,
# so no port. Its token writes placement only — `vms/workers/*`, `vms/placement/*`, `vms/slots/*`
# (`SPEC.acl_controller()`) and the snapshot object — and never a camera's row. Checked by
# `tests/test_deploy_units.py`, which also asserts it mounts neither the archive nor the spool.
#
# ## Stanza by stanza
#
# ### `[Unit]`
# - `Description=VMS controller — the only writer of placement`
# - `After=network.target` — ordering only.
#
# ### `[Container]`
# - `Image=localhost/vmsserver:latest` — the shared image.
# - `Exec=python3 -m vms controller` — the `controller` verb: `VmsController` over a `FileVariables` opened as
#   writer `vmscontroller` with the controller ACL.
# - `EnvironmentFile=/data/config/vms.env` — it needs `PLATFORM_DIR` (the stores), `CAPACITY` (the fallback
#   for a worker whose heartbeat says nothing) and `LOG_LEVEL`; the rest of the file is harmless to it.
# - `Volume=/data/platform:/data/platform:z` — the only mount: the config store for rows, assignments,
#   placement, slots and the object store for heartbeats (read) and the snapshot (write). No `/data/archive`,
#   no `/data/spool`: "the ACL says which rows each token writes; the mounts say which bytes" — the controller
#   has no bytes to write. `test_who_may_write_where_is_in_the_mounts_too` asserts both are absent.
# - `Network=host` — nothing listens; kept for symmetry and for М11's stores.
#
# ### `[Service]`
# - `Restart=always` — a crash loses nothing: every pass reads the store, decides, writes by CAS. Recording
#   continues while it is down (`test_the_failure_arithmetic`; "the controller is never on the recovery
#   path").
# - `RestartSec=2`.
#
# ### `[Install]`
# - `WantedBy=multi-user.target` — starts at boot.
#
# ## Notes
# - No `count` and no scheduler client: how many workers exist is systemd's (`vmsworker@…` instances) or
#   Nomad's; the controller only reads their heartbeats and the `released` flag on slots.
# - Two of these running against one store are harmless (`test_two_controllers_agree_by_cas`), so a restart
#   overlapping an old instance needs no lock.
# ================================================================================================
[Unit]
Description=VMS controller — the only writer of placement
After=network.target

[Container]
Image=localhost/vmsserver:latest
Exec=python3 -m vms controller
EnvironmentFile=/data/config/vms.env
Volume=/data/platform:/data/platform:z
Network=host

[Service]
Restart=always
RestartSec=2

[Install]
WantedBy=multi-user.target
